<!-- ═══ COMPARE ═══ -->
<div class="sec" id="sec-compare">
<div class="card">
<h2>⚖️ Comparison: Computing Across Eras</h2>
<table class="tbl">
<thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Abacus (2400 BC)</th><th>ENIAC (1945)</th><th>Smartphone (2024)</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><strong>Speed</strong></td><td>~10 ops/min (human)</td><td>5,000 ops/sec</td><td>Billions/sec</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Size</strong></td><td>Fits in one hand</td><td>Fills a large room (1800 sq ft)</td><td>Fits in a pocket</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Weight</strong></td><td>~500 g</td><td>~30,000 kg</td><td>~170 g</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Power needed</strong></td><td>None (manual)</td><td>150,000 watts</td><td>~5 watts</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Storage</strong></td><td>None</td><td>Punched cards</td><td>256 GB+</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Cost</strong></td><td>A few dollars</td><td>$400,000 (1940s)</td><td>$200–$1,000</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Users</strong></td><td>Anyone</td><td>Trained engineers only</td><td>4+ billion people</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<div class="note">📱 Your smartphone is <strong>1 million times more powerful</strong> than ENIAC — and fits in your pocket. Computing has advanced more in 80 years than almost any other technology in human history!</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h2>🏆 Famous People in Computer History</h2>
<div class="wiki-row"><div class="wiki-item">
<img src="./generation-timeline_files/480px-Alan_Turing_Aged_16.jpg" alt="Alan Turing — Father of Theoretical Computer Science and AI" class="zoomable" data-author="Unknown" data-license="Public Domain" data-source="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alan_Turing_Aged_16.jpg" data-source-label="Wikimedia Commons">
<div class="wiki-item-cap">Alan Turing (age 16)</div></div><div class="wiki-item">
<img src="./generation-timeline_files/480px-John_von_Neumann.jpg" alt="John von Neumann — designed the architecture used in all modern computers" class="zoomable" data-author="LANL" data-license="Public Domain" data-source="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_von_Neumann.jpg" data-source-label="Wikimedia Commons">
<div class="wiki-item-cap">John von Neumann</div></div><div class="wiki-item">
<img src="./generation-timeline_files/480px-Gracehopper.agr.jpg" alt="Grace Hopper — invented the first compiler and coined the term " debugging""="" class="zoomable" data-author="Unknown" data-license="Public Domain" data-source="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gracehopper.agr.jpg" data-source-label="Wikimedia Commons">
<div class="wiki-item-cap">Grace Hopper</div></div></div>
<div class="cmp-grid">
  <div class="cmp-box blue"><div class="cmp-tag">Alan Turing (1912–1954)</div><h3>Father of AI</h3><p>Invented the Turing Machine — the theoretical model of all computers. Proposed the Turing Test for machine intelligence. Broke Nazi codes in WW2.</p></div>
  <div class="cmp-box grn"><div class="cmp-tag">Grace Hopper (1906–1992)</div><h3>First Compiler</h3><p>Created the first compiler (translates code to machine language). Coined "debugging" after finding a real moth stuck in a relay. Rear Admiral in US Navy.</p></div>
  <div class="cmp-box pur"><div class="cmp-tag">John von Neumann (1903–1957)</div><h3>von Neumann Architecture</h3><p>Designed the stored-program concept — programs stored in memory alongside data. ALL modern computers use von Neumann Architecture.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div><!-- /compare -->

