<!-- ═══ SUMMARY ═══ -->
<div class="sec" id="sec-sum">
<div class="card">
<h2>📋 Key Points Summary</h2>
<div class="sum-grid">
  <div class="sum-box"><div class="sum-term">Abacus (~2400 BC)</div><div class="sum-def">World's first calculating tool. Uses beads on rods. Origin: China.</div></div>
  <div class="sum-box"><div class="sum-term">Pascaline (1642)</div><div class="sum-def">First mechanical calculator. Invented by Blaise Pascal. Could add and subtract.</div></div>
  <div class="sum-box"><div class="sum-term">Charles Babbage</div><div class="sum-def">Father of the Computer. Designed Difference Engine (1822) and Analytical Engine (1837).</div></div>
  <div class="sum-box"><div class="sum-term">Ada Lovelace</div><div class="sum-def">World's first programmer. Wrote first algorithm for Babbage's Analytical Engine (1843).</div></div>
  <div class="sum-box"><div class="sum-term">ENIAC (1945)</div><div class="sum-def">First general-purpose electronic computer. Used 18,000 vacuum tubes. Weighed 30 tons.</div></div>
  <div class="sum-box"><div class="sum-term">5 Generations</div><div class="sum-def">1st: Vacuum tubes · 2nd: Transistors · 3rd: IC · 4th: Microprocessors · 5th: AI</div></div>
  <div class="sum-box"><div class="sum-term">Binary System</div><div class="sum-def">All computers store data as 0s and 1s (binary digits/bits). Invented by Leibniz (1671).</div></div>
  <div class="sum-box"><div class="sum-term">WWW (1989)</div><div class="sum-def">World Wide Web invented by Tim Berners-Lee at CERN. Changed global communication forever.</div></div>
</div>
<div class="activity">
  <div class="activity-hd">🎯 Research Activity</div>
  <p>Find out: What computing devices exist in your school, home, and local area? Make a list and try to identify which generation each belongs to. Share your findings with the class!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div><!-- /sum -->



